      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would really help with immersion as well. Anytime I'm locomoting as an avatar that's under like 4ft, the world seems like it's zooming by impossibly fast. \n\n(And the default move speed is a bit faster than I'd like imo, but that's another topic altogether)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-10T01:24:32.942Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With scaling added to the game as a base feature, it's easy to notice that when becoming very tiny, it can be difficult to move around with precision as the movement speed isn't adjusted at all. This is easy to notice in some worlds which are already adding tiny zones for scaled players to hang out in. I think a possible solution would be a toggle in the expressions menu, next to scaling; scale movement speed based on size. If you shrink yourself, you could then optionally move slower, as determined by your height.\n\nThere might be concerns about cheating or breaking experiences in some worlds, so perhaps by default there's a movement speed cap set to the current default movement speed (so players can only go slower, not faster.) Additionally, perhaps world authors could be able to define minimum and maximum speeds as needed.",
